WEBVTT

00:02.569 --> 00:05.834
<i>[Singing] It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.939 --> 00:09.204
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.309 --> 00:12.745
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.846 --> 00:15.474
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.982 --> 00:18.746
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.352 --> 00:22.515
<i>Lucky there's a man who
Positively can do</i>

00:22.622 --> 00:24.180
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.290 --> 00:25.780
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.959 --> 00:30.760
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:34.501 --> 00:36.662
Okay, now, don't wander too far, kids.

00:36.770 --> 00:40.331
You know, more children get kidnapped
at the grocery store than anywhere else.

00:45.278 --> 00:47.337
- Hey.
- You got me!

00:47.747 --> 00:50.272
- Not quick enough.
- Not quick enough, no.

00:50.383 --> 00:53.181
- No, I was close, though.
- You were close.

00:55.121 --> 00:56.918
I'm gonna go get some oranges, Stewie.

00:57.023 --> 00:59.116
Here, hold the rest of these bags
for Mommy.

00:59.492 --> 01:03.394
What brilliant parenting, Lois.
Leave a tiny infant with a plastic bag.

01:03.496 --> 01:06.363
You know, I might asphyxiate myself,
just to teach you a lesson.

01:06.466 --> 01:09.162
Here I go, just like that boy from INXS.

01:10.170 --> 01:12.365
I am going to do it.

01:14.474 --> 01:16.135
Blast! Good Lord, Lois...

01:16.242 --> 01:18.642
either I was a C-section
or you're Wonder Woman.

01:18.745 --> 01:22.681
Chris, would you run and get some milk?
And be sure to take it from the back.

02:05.458 --> 02:08.325
- Chris, where have you been?
- I don't know.

02:10.430 --> 02:14.298
- $53.98.
- Oh no, I forgot to go to the bank.

02:14.400 --> 02:17.096
I'm a little short.
I'll have to put the ham back.

02:25.011 --> 02:27.912
You know, I got some candy in my van,
if your kid wants some.

02:28.014 --> 02:29.140
Oh, great!

02:29.816 --> 02:34.048
- Wait a second!
- You got me! You got me.

02:34.721 --> 02:37.849
- I'll get him, though. I'll get him.
- I bet you will. I bet you will.

02:44.130 --> 02:46.394
Is that ham? I thought you put that back.

02:46.499 --> 02:47.659
Oh...

02:48.134 --> 02:51.570
- No, I put the other ham back.
- I don't remember another ham.

02:51.671 --> 02:53.832
<i>Well, you were too busy
eyeballing that Redbook...</i>

02:53.940 --> 02:57.432
- with Glenn Close on the cover.
- Hey, she is a handsome woman.

02:57.544 --> 03:01.844
Well, well! Look who's carrying a little
flame for Glenn Close. What a surprise!

03:01.948 --> 03:04.314
Although it's not the first time
you've surprised me.

03:04.417 --> 03:06.146
I have so much stuff to do today.

03:06.252 --> 03:08.243
I have to do laundry,
then I have a piano lesson...

03:08.354 --> 03:10.720
then I have to make dinner. I am so busy.
Better hurry.

03:10.823 --> 03:12.654
Lois, I want my graham...

03:13.493 --> 03:14.460
Oh.

03:15.628 --> 03:18.756
- Hey.
- Hey.

03:19.666 --> 03:21.634
Playing a little dress-up?

03:23.269 --> 03:26.898
- Yeah.
- Yeah, good.

03:27.207 --> 03:28.970
It's fun to pretend.

03:29.209 --> 03:32.007
- So listen, if you see Lois tell her...
- Graham cracker.

03:32.111 --> 03:34.238
Graham cracker, yes, yes. That's it.

03:35.448 --> 03:37.245
All right, so...

03:37.717 --> 03:41.949
I'm just gonna go out in the hallway
and throw up about something else.

03:46.025 --> 03:47.549
This is cute.

03:48.561 --> 03:49.550
Oh, my God.

03:54.067 --> 03:55.659
[Laughing maniacally]

04:08.248 --> 04:10.409
Oh, my God, that was such a rush.

04:11.451 --> 04:14.079
Yeah. I'm alive!

04:17.056 --> 04:19.957
- Thanks for having us over.
- Yeah, it's a wonderful dinner.

04:20.059 --> 04:24.359
And on this beautiful new china.
You guys have a lot of new stuff.

04:24.464 --> 04:27.922
- Yeah, Lois has been splurging her ass off.
- Yeah, she has.

04:28.034 --> 04:29.661
You know, she bought me
something yesterday...

04:29.769 --> 04:33.330
but I am not going to tell you what it is.
I want you to guess. Just close your eyes.

04:35.642 --> 04:38.270
- It's a soccer horn.
- I know what it is!

04:38.478 --> 04:40.810
Hey, is that an original Matisse?

04:40.913 --> 04:44.007
Hey, Bonnie. Listen, why don't you stop
with the questions, huh?

04:44.117 --> 04:45.982
You're ruining everyone's good time.

04:46.085 --> 04:49.077
Like Peter did, when he used to entertain
terminally ill kids.

04:49.188 --> 04:50.712
Hi there. How you all doing?

04:50.823 --> 04:55.192
All right, so I'm at the DMV the other day.
Long lines. Long lines at the DMV.

04:55.295 --> 04:57.991
But you'll find out all about that
when you get...

04:59.732 --> 05:00.892
[Stammering]

05:01.100 --> 05:04.592
Moving on. So I finally tried Viagra and...

05:04.704 --> 05:05.671
[Boy groaning]

05:05.838 --> 05:07.931
We got a joker in the audience there.

05:08.041 --> 05:10.771
You got something
you want to say, there, Mr. Heckler?

05:10.877 --> 05:12.606
Dying hurts.

05:12.712 --> 05:15.010
Tell me about it.
So anyway, who hates flying?

05:23.022 --> 05:23.989
[Brian clearing his throat]

05:24.157 --> 05:27.684
- Brian, what are you doing here?
- I should ask you the same question.

05:27.794 --> 05:30.695
Lois, you're in an auto parts store,
stealing mufflers.

05:30.797 --> 05:33.231
This is worse than
that Winona Ryder thing.

05:33.333 --> 05:34.823
Are you saying I am a klepto?

05:34.934 --> 05:37.164
<i>Actually, I was talking about
The Age of Innocence.</i>

05:37.270 --> 05:39.795
It is settled, May.
Our parents have consented...

05:39.906 --> 05:43.774
and you and I are to be married
on the first warm, sunny day of spring.

05:43.876 --> 05:47.812
That would be most good, Newland,
most good.

05:48.548 --> 05:51.642
I am sorry, but she is just awful.
Is there any way...

05:51.751 --> 05:54.049
I mean, can we add, like,
a topless scene, or something?

05:54.153 --> 05:55.415
- Yeah.
- Really?

05:55.521 --> 05:58.649
- Yeah.
- We can? Great. All right, we got a movie.

05:59.192 --> 06:01.854
God, you're right, Brian,
I'm out of control...

06:01.961 --> 06:05.829
but I don't know what to do.
I'm just hooked on the rush of shoplifting.

06:06.099 --> 06:08.499
I haven't felt a thrill like this
in a long time.

06:08.601 --> 06:12.002
Well, I think you've had enough thrills.
Why don't you just put everything back?

06:12.638 --> 06:16.130
Okay, Brian.
You know, you really are a good friend.

06:16.242 --> 06:18.073
Let me rub your belly.

06:19.312 --> 06:20.802
[Brian moaning in ecstasy]

06:26.219 --> 06:27.584
Put it back.

06:32.458 --> 06:34.688
<i>Welcome back to Channel 5 News at 10:00.</i>

06:34.794 --> 06:35.783
<i>For those of you wondering...</i>

06:35.895 --> 06:38.125
<i>what I've been writing down
as we go to commercial...</i>

06:38.231 --> 06:40.461
<i>it's a cat. Just a cat.</i>

06:40.800 --> 06:43.234
<i>In other news, police are still looking
for the culprit...</i>

06:43.336 --> 06:46.669
<i>who stole a valuable Matisse painting
from the Quahog Museum of Art.</i>

06:47.240 --> 06:49.572
A Matisse painting?

06:49.709 --> 06:51.336
<i>Also, scientists announced today...</i>

06:51.444 --> 06:54.675
<i>that if your hand is bigger than your face,
you have cancer.</i>

06:54.914 --> 06:55.903
Ha. Ha.

06:56.015 --> 06:59.678
<i>Got you. That's not even really news.</i>

07:02.488 --> 07:03.819
[Imitating a car]

07:04.323 --> 07:06.314
Oh no, Rupert, we're out of gas.

07:06.426 --> 07:10.453
We better ask directions at that creepy,
and possibly haunted, house.

07:11.931 --> 07:14.399
A ghost! It's okay. It's okay.

07:14.500 --> 07:16.229
We got away just in time.

07:17.837 --> 07:19.998
All right, now,
is that everything you stole?

07:20.106 --> 07:21.198
That's everything.

07:21.307 --> 07:23.673
You know, you really should talk
to a therapist about this.

07:23.776 --> 07:25.243
I mean, it really helped Peter out...

07:25.344 --> 07:27.539
when he became obsessed
with that fantasy world of his.

07:32.585 --> 07:34.052
Yeah!

07:34.320 --> 07:37.153
- You're a little too heavy, buddy.
- Yeah!

07:38.090 --> 07:40.581
- We're going down.
- Yeah!

07:42.895 --> 07:44.385
Yeah.

07:44.630 --> 07:45.995
You know, Lois, we're just lucky...

07:46.098 --> 07:48.396
we got this under control
before the police caught onto you.

07:48.501 --> 07:50.765
Hold it right there, Lois,
you are under arrest.

07:50.870 --> 07:55.330
Oh, crap. All right, look, just take it easy,
Joe. All right, Lois will go peacefully.

07:55.441 --> 07:59.036
Oh, my God, I am so embarrassed.
Let me just get my purse.

08:00.480 --> 08:01.469
[Laughing maniacally]

08:01.581 --> 08:02.809
Sucker!

08:24.036 --> 08:27.130
Sorry, Lois. Regulations.
I can't give you any special treatment.

08:27.240 --> 08:30.266
- It's okay, Joe, I understand.
- Shut up, maggot!

08:35.715 --> 08:38.912
Your Honor, I am so sorry
for stealing all that stuff.

08:39.018 --> 08:40.679
I just couldn't control myself.

08:40.786 --> 08:43.653
Well, Mrs. Griffin,
considering this is your first offense...

08:43.756 --> 08:46.953
I've decided to go lenient and...
Where the hell is my gavel?

08:47.059 --> 08:48.492
[Giggling sheepishly]

08:49.395 --> 08:50.419
Give me that.

08:50.530 --> 08:53.363
I sentence you to two years
in the State Prison.

08:53.466 --> 08:55.957
- Man, that is bogus.
- Order in the court!

08:56.068 --> 08:59.196
Another outburst like that, Mr. Griffin,
and I'll extend the sentence.

08:59.672 --> 09:01.572
- Okay, three years.
- That was a sneeze.

09:01.674 --> 09:02.766
- Four years.
- I am sorry.

09:02.875 --> 09:04.399
- Five years.
- You douchebag.

09:04.510 --> 09:08.071
- All right, three years it is.
- Three years in prison?

09:08.180 --> 09:10.080
Oh, my God, what have I done?

09:10.182 --> 09:14.915
<i>Oh, man, I haven't been this upset
since I watched The Blob on television.</i>

09:15.254 --> 09:19.156
Look out behind you, lady! It's the Blob!
I'll save you.

09:23.529 --> 09:25.997
Here you go. Meet your new friends.

09:27.800 --> 09:31.759
- Hi, I'm Lois.
- I'm Fisty, that's Stabby, and that's Balls.

09:31.871 --> 09:34.772
- Pull up a chair, we're playing cards.
- Oh. Okay.

09:35.908 --> 09:39.207
- So, are those biblical names?
- Yeah, Fisty is.

09:41.847 --> 09:43.314
Boy, I sure miss Lois.

09:43.416 --> 09:45.646
I wish she was here
to clean up all this stuff.

09:45.751 --> 09:47.275
- Hey, what's this?
- Mustard.

09:47.386 --> 09:49.479
Oh, that's right.
We had hot dogs last week.

09:50.122 --> 09:53.717
- You gonna eat that?
- The mustard on your shoulder? No.

09:55.361 --> 09:58.330
Kids, look! Look. A deer.

09:58.431 --> 10:01.628
- Can we pet him?
- No, no. Just watch.

10:04.804 --> 10:05.964
[Sighing]

10:06.172 --> 10:08.766
Peter!

10:10.009 --> 10:12.477
There's so much doody in here.

10:14.180 --> 10:16.148
I can't take it any more.

10:16.349 --> 10:18.249
I haven't eaten in four days...

10:18.351 --> 10:22.754
'cause I just can't fit any more in there.

10:23.489 --> 10:24.683
Help me.

10:27.226 --> 10:29.694
Okay, now when we get
to your mother's cage, say hello...

10:29.795 --> 10:32.423
but don't drag your ass,
'cause I want to go the reptile house.

10:32.531 --> 10:36.160
- And we got to see those pandas.
- Peter, this isn't a zoo, it's a prison.

10:36.268 --> 10:39.101
- Quagmire, what are you doing here?
- It's conjugal visit day.

10:39.205 --> 10:42.504
You know, I love doing a woman in the can.
Oh, giggidy, giggidy, goo!

10:42.642 --> 10:45.042
Who else but Quagmire?

10:45.144 --> 10:47.271
<i>[Singing] He's Quagmire
Quagmire</i>

10:47.413 --> 10:49.745
<i>You never really know
what he's gonna do next</i>

10:49.849 --> 10:52.113
<i>He's Quagmire
Quagmire</i>

10:52.251 --> 10:53.479
Giggidy, giggidy, giggidy.

10:53.586 --> 10:54.746
<i>Let's have sex</i>

10:54.854 --> 10:58.813
I do hope nothing happens
to spoil this fancy dinner party.

10:59.992 --> 11:02.825
Giggidy, giggidy, giggidy, giggidy, giggidy,
giggidy, giggidy, goo.

11:03.262 --> 11:05.389
Who else but Quagmire?

11:05.765 --> 11:08.290
<i>He's Quagmire
Quagmire</i>

11:08.401 --> 11:09.891
Giggidy, giggidy, goo.

11:10.536 --> 11:13.801
Oh, it is so good to see all of you.
How is everything at home?

11:13.906 --> 11:17.171
It's horrible, Lois. I've had to do
all the things that you usually do.

11:17.276 --> 11:19.744
Like the other night,
I had to go to your book club meeting.

11:19.845 --> 11:23.781
I really admired the mother character's
admission of personal torment...

11:23.883 --> 11:26.477
- after her daughter's death.
- I disagree.

11:26.585 --> 11:28.815
I felt a total lack of ethical integrity...

11:28.921 --> 11:32.379
in her readiness to abandon her children
and start a life of her own.

11:32.491 --> 11:35.483
Here's another thing:
The book can also be...

11:36.095 --> 11:37.255
a hat.

11:37.396 --> 11:39.455
And the other night, I had to do a...

11:39.565 --> 11:43.023
Well, you know, that thing that you
usually do for me every Thursday night.

11:52.178 --> 11:55.636
I can't believe you're serving
a three-year sentence, it seems so harsh.

11:55.748 --> 11:59.878
The only upside is that it's given me time
to think about why I ended up in here.

11:59.985 --> 12:04.251
I guess I was stealing, because
I was so sick of the same old routine.

12:04.590 --> 12:07.320
I felt like I had a void in my life.

12:07.426 --> 12:09.917
- Like, there was a secret hole in me.
- Oh, God!

12:10.029 --> 12:14.932
And I was trying to fill that hole with
all kinds of expensive objects and things.

12:15.134 --> 12:16.567
Oh, God!

12:16.669 --> 12:20.264
And I felt wonderful
with all those things filling that hole.

12:20.372 --> 12:21.600
Oh, God!

12:21.874 --> 12:23.364
I did this to myself...

12:23.476 --> 12:27.344
so I'm just gonna have to lay back and
let the penal system teach me a lesson.

12:27.446 --> 12:29.243
That one is also sexual.

12:29.381 --> 12:32.111
Well, I guess with good behavior,
you could be out in two years.

12:32.218 --> 12:34.516
I made my own bed with this one, guys.

12:34.620 --> 12:37.088
I'm just gonna have to pay my debt
to society.

12:37.189 --> 12:41.683
Not necessarily. I think I got an idea
of how to smuggle you out.

12:41.961 --> 12:44.828
Bye-bye, take care, now. Have a nice day.

12:44.930 --> 12:45.897
[Peter mumbling]

12:54.039 --> 12:55.506
What do we do?

12:57.476 --> 12:59.637
Hurry! We'll hide in that van.

13:07.186 --> 13:09.450
My God, you know what this means?

13:09.555 --> 13:13.491
- You're all accessories to my escape.
- She's right. We're fugitives from the law.

13:13.592 --> 13:16.060
- What the hell is wrong with you?
- I'm a dog, all right.

13:16.228 --> 13:19.061
I have a very tough time
standing up in the car.

13:19.165 --> 13:22.430
Well, then we're fugitives.
But at least the family's back together.

13:22.535 --> 13:24.526
- I wonder where we're going.
- Calm down!

13:24.637 --> 13:26.127
I'll tell you what were going to do.

13:26.238 --> 13:29.401
Wherever this van stops,
we'll begin a new life together.

13:29.508 --> 13:31.942
We'll blend in
to the fabric of that community.

13:35.614 --> 13:37.605
Peter, we're in Asiantown.

13:38.951 --> 13:42.148
Well, at least I don't have to worry
about the evil monkey here.

13:48.093 --> 13:51.551
If we're gonna hide out here in Asiantown
we have to find a place to live.

13:51.664 --> 13:55.532
Yes, and we should do nothing to draw
attention to ourselves as outsiders.

13:55.634 --> 13:57.568
Oh, my God! It's Jackie Chan.

13:58.137 --> 13:59.900
Oh, my God! It's Jackie Chan.

14:00.372 --> 14:02.067
Oh, my God! It's Jackie Chan.

14:02.174 --> 14:04.574
Hi there!
Always nice to meet a fan of my movies.

14:04.677 --> 14:07.168
- My God, you're Ethan Hawke!
- No, I'm not.

14:07.279 --> 14:10.146
Sorry, my mistake.
My God, it's Ethan Hawke!

14:10.249 --> 14:13.412
- Mom, can we go get some food?
- My God, there's Malcolm in middle!

14:13.519 --> 14:15.646
- I'm not a boy.
- Yes, you are.

14:20.392 --> 14:23.486
- I can't believe we have to live here.
- This sucks!

14:23.963 --> 14:27.421
Tell me about it. I haven't seen
one female baby since we got here.

14:27.533 --> 14:29.057
This place is a sausage-fest.

14:29.168 --> 14:32.797
Come on, kids, we've been through worse.
Meg, you remember when you found out...

14:32.905 --> 14:34.702
your gynecologist
never finished med school?

14:34.807 --> 14:37.571
All right, Meg,
let's take a look at that bergina.

14:38.010 --> 14:40.672
But Peter, how are we going to support
ourselves here?

14:40.779 --> 14:44.647
We'll all have to get jobs, but I'm sure
we'll each find something we can do.

14:46.118 --> 14:47.813
- Where are you from?
- Tokyo.

14:47.953 --> 14:50.683
Tokyo! Yeah, it's a great town.

14:50.890 --> 14:52.585
- Lot of people, though.
- Yup.

14:52.691 --> 14:55.251
You're here on business?
I bet its business...

14:55.361 --> 14:57.921
'cause I had a fare earlier today that...

14:58.364 --> 15:01.765
This used to be a people business,
but now, I don't know.

15:04.603 --> 15:08.767
Damn! I say, I seem to have sewn
a shoe to my hand, may I go to the nurse?

15:08.874 --> 15:10.239
Replace him!

15:16.282 --> 15:17.271
Faster!

15:17.750 --> 15:22.312
So, what exactly would you say
qualifies you to work as a sumo wrestler?

15:22.421 --> 15:25.913
Oh, are you kidding?
I'm a born athlete, just like Greg Louganis.

15:26.158 --> 15:27.591
Hi, I'm Peter Griffin.

15:27.693 --> 15:30.628
You're probably asking yourself,
"Which way are they gonna go?

15:30.729 --> 15:33.391
"Are they gonna make
a diving-board head-injury joke?

15:33.499 --> 15:35.262
"Are they gonna make an AIDS joke?

15:35.367 --> 15:37.494
"Or are they gonna make a joke
about the fact...

15:37.603 --> 15:40.128
"that his last name
sounds suspiciously like 'anus'?"

15:40.239 --> 15:43.902
Well, we're gonna take the high road
and do a no-body-hair joke.

15:44.009 --> 15:47.240
- Brian?
- Hi, I'm Greg Louganis. I'm totally shaven.

15:47.346 --> 15:49.507
Terrific! Terrific.

15:52.818 --> 15:54.911
Damn it, Swanson. I want them found.

15:55.020 --> 15:58.319
Mayor West, we have every available man
looking for the Griffins.

15:58.424 --> 15:59.721
We just don't have any leads.

15:59.825 --> 16:01.520
Not the Griffins, you moron!

16:01.660 --> 16:05.619
The rest of my Lite Brite pieces!
My name isn't "Adam We"!

16:06.432 --> 16:09.993
Or is it? Who am I?
What number did you dial?

16:10.102 --> 16:13.538
Don't ever call here again.
I guess I told him!

16:14.006 --> 16:16.804
Nobody messes with Adam We.

16:17.042 --> 16:18.805
<i>And now, ladies and gentlemen...</i>

16:18.911 --> 16:22.014
<i>Sumo Tonight,
brought to you by Asian Trix.</i>

16:22.314 --> 16:24.544
Silly rabbit! Trix are for kids!

16:24.650 --> 16:26.015
You share!

16:29.588 --> 16:32.113
I'm not really sure what to do here.

16:33.025 --> 16:35.391
Boy! You've put on weight, Jackie Chan.

16:37.229 --> 16:39.459
JOE: Oh, my God!
BONNIE: Did you walk?

16:50.075 --> 16:51.042
Oh...

16:52.044 --> 16:56.071
<i>MAN: You're watching CBS ASIANTOWN.</i>

16:56.315 --> 16:58.977
- Hey, everybody, I'm home.
- Oh, you're just in time.

16:59.084 --> 17:00.847
I ordered Caucasian for dinner.

17:00.953 --> 17:03.786
Chris, I'm hungry.
It's your turn to keep watch for the cops.

17:03.889 --> 17:06.289
Wait a minute,
am I the only one who thinks this is nuts?

17:06.392 --> 17:07.882
We've given up our whole lives.

17:07.993 --> 17:10.393
Come on, Brian,
a change of scenery is always good.

17:10.496 --> 17:13.226
Yes, I thoroughly enjoyed
my trip to Nebraska.

17:18.637 --> 17:22.095
So, anybody see any good movies lately?

17:22.241 --> 17:23.868
- No, not really.
- No.

17:25.411 --> 17:26.878
Read any good books?

17:26.979 --> 17:28.241
No.

17:29.815 --> 17:31.180
Anything new with corn?

17:31.283 --> 17:32.807
- Yeah, corn...
- Corn...

17:32.918 --> 17:34.909
- You betcha!
- Corn...

17:35.020 --> 17:36.612
- Yeah.
- Corn is always interesting.

17:37.022 --> 17:39.991
Hey, Mom, Mr. Swanson's here to visit us.

17:40.092 --> 17:41.059
What?

17:44.163 --> 17:46.461
Oh, my God, we got to get out of here!

17:50.702 --> 17:52.966
Taxi! Follow that family.

18:03.115 --> 18:05.549
Come on, everybody, over the fence.

18:06.018 --> 18:09.317
Ah, yes, a fence.
The cripple's natural enemy.

18:14.493 --> 18:16.222
I think we lost him.

18:18.097 --> 18:20.861
- There they are.
- Quick! Into the sewer.

18:26.004 --> 18:30.270
- Good Lord! It's disgusting down here.
- Boy, Stewie's got the right idea.

18:30.809 --> 18:33.573
- What the hell are you doing?
- It's wet down there, Brian.

18:33.679 --> 18:37.240
This sucks worse than that time
I did cocaine with Karl Malden.

18:37.416 --> 18:39.316
What are you getting
all bent out of shape about?

18:39.418 --> 18:42.615
Well, you know, Karl, I didn't get...
I got virtually nothing here, you know?

18:42.721 --> 18:43.949
Look, I don't see what the problem is.

18:44.056 --> 18:45.546
No, you wouldn't, would you?

18:45.657 --> 18:47.955
Look, all I'm saying is,
I got the raw end of the deal.

18:48.060 --> 18:50.585
- You invited me over.
- Yeah, well, now I'm regretting it.

18:54.533 --> 18:56.160
When I fire rockets...

18:56.268 --> 18:59.704
I always pretend
I shooting at Alan Alda and Jamie Farr.

18:59.805 --> 19:02.535
Take that, wisecracking meatball surgeon!

19:17.322 --> 19:20.189
- Which way should we go?
- I don't know, let's ask the Goonies.

19:20.292 --> 19:23.693
- Take the left one.
- Thanks. Hey, Chunk, come here.

19:23.996 --> 19:26.794
Before you go, do the truffle shuffle.

19:27.266 --> 19:30.326
- Oh, come on!
- Do the truffle shuffle.

19:35.541 --> 19:37.338
Childhood obesity.

19:39.945 --> 19:42.345
Lois, come on, what are you doing?

19:42.814 --> 19:45.374
- I can't do it, Peter.
- What are you talking about?

19:45.484 --> 19:49.250
Look at us? We're running
through a sewer, and it's because of me.

19:49.354 --> 19:52.118
Look, honey, it was very sweet of you
to break me out of jail...

19:52.224 --> 19:53.885
but I did something wrong.

19:53.992 --> 19:57.257
And I'm the one who should pay,
not my whole family.

19:59.031 --> 20:00.999
I'm gonna turn myself in.

20:03.168 --> 20:04.999
You're mine now, Lois!

20:06.104 --> 20:07.298
[Joe screaming]

20:09.408 --> 20:10.898
Oh, my God, Joe!

20:11.977 --> 20:14.844
Joe, you're too heavy. I can't hang on.

20:15.047 --> 20:17.242
Pretend I'm your child, Lois.

20:17.616 --> 20:18.583
Not Meg! Not Meg!

20:21.553 --> 20:24.249
Lois, you saved my life.

20:25.090 --> 20:28.082
I say, Corey Haim!
Are you with the Goonies as well?

20:28.193 --> 20:30.684
No, I just live down here. Mine!

20:34.566 --> 20:37.399
It was so nice of Joe to work things out
with that judge.

20:37.502 --> 20:40.300
Yeah, but I'm sure gonna miss my buddies
down at the sumo ring.

20:40.405 --> 20:42.965
Dad, can you teach me
how to sumo wrestle?

20:43.075 --> 20:45.600
It's not too hard, Chris.
Brian, help me demonstrate.

20:45.711 --> 20:48.646
- Peter, maybe somebody else could...
- Come on!

20:49.581 --> 20:52.573
Okay, so on the count to three,
you try to push me out of the ring...

20:52.684 --> 20:54.584
I try to push you out of the ring.
Okay? Ready?

20:54.686 --> 20:56.244
One, two, three!

20:58.090 --> 20:59.887
What the hell? What the hell?

21:00.726 --> 21:03.092
- Brian, I'm sorry...
- No! No. You know what?

21:03.195 --> 21:05.390
It's not cool, Peter. It's not cool.

21:05.391 --> 22:06.391
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru